593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167700 #edb/ref 1061 32692 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167700 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a9dbf529-bcef-5ee9-8535-112f0fae57f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167700 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186168090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167711 #edb/ref 1061 32719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167711 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "143b8be3-52fa-5eb8-99d4-c0ff1ef2dbfd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167711 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186168101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168090 #edb/ref 1064 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe derivatives of the reciprocal hyperbolic functions are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x) & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) & =-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) & =-{csch}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's use these results to find the derivative of \n\n$$\ny= \\sech x - 2\\csch x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating term-by-term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x-2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-2(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168090 #edb/ref 1065 5208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168090 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "9f94990a-0da5-522a-9d5f-7e0b269b50ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168090 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168101 #edb/ref 1064 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$ \n\nWe wish to prove the following result:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\sech{x}) = -\\sech{x} \\tanh{x}.\n$$\n\nTo do this, we can use the fact that\n\n$$\n\\sech x = \\dfrac{1}{\\cosh x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equation using the chain rule, we arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)}^{-1} \\\\  & =-{(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)}^{-2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can prove the results for the derivatives of the hyperbolic cosecant and cotangent in a similar way." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168101 #edb/ref 1065 5226 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168101 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "cb6ff220-98cb-5e8a-8a09-958d158b0d10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168101 #edb/ref 1067 "Deriving the Result for the Derivative of the Hyperbolic Secant" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
